\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec2 \'93Hey Torin!\'94 says Mira
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93How\'92re you doing Mira?\'94 asked Torin
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Nothing new. The usual please\'94, she replied
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Coming right up. Have you heard that the tank\'92s president is being replaced?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93No, do you know who the successor is?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93I think she was called President Veyr\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93She? That\'92s new\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Here\'92s your tuna sandwich, and yes, it is.\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93You know, I can\'92t wait to see what else th-\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Wait, Mira, look at the time\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Oh sharks! It's 9:20, I've got to go, bye Torin!\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93See you tomorrow Mira!\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira rushed to the school elevator, usually when residents of the tank decided pto move up or down in levels, or even from one level to another, as Mira did every day to get to school in the middle rank. They had to take the massive spiral staircase that went throughout all the levels of the tank, right in the center of it, doubling as a support column for the tank.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She rushed through the streets, rushing up the stairs of \'91The Archimedes school of The Silo\'92, she ran to their personal cubicles, using her student card to open her own, the same she used to access the elevators to go from the third level of the Tank to the second. Just as she was about to rush into class she bumped into Ocean, her most trusted friend for as long as Mira could remember.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Hey\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Come on Ocean we\'92re late for History of society! And you know Mrs. Rivers does not tolerate tardiness\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Class hasn\'92t even started yet Mira, workers came in to change President Kennedy\'92s class portrait for Presidents Veyr\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Oh\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 With the shocking news of the change of administration just that morning, Mira had forgotten about that unsettling portrait that every president of the Tank had in all the classes of the three schools, she had never even heard of President Veyr before the news, much less seen her, she wondered if she would have the same gigantic nose as President Kennedy, not that she could ever come to on it outside of the safety of her room with Ocean, everyone in the tank knew what the punishment for disrespecting the President was, being sent to the surface, where death would happen in just a few seconds.
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 P
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Girls! You may enter the class now\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mrs. Rivers said at the doorway of her classroom, both of them walked to the schoolroom, most of her schoolmates were already sitting at their desks. Mira's eyes instantly travelled to the portrait on top of the board, the teacher clapped once, and they all stood up, bringing both of her hands behind her back, and her feet exactly shoulder length apart. The only correct stand when singing the national anthem, one they had been taught relentlessly as children. She clapped once more, and they all simultaneously started singing.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Then suddenly, the room's fluorescent lighting went completely dark, Mira looked up, it was uncommon for the power to go out in the Tank, but it wasn\'92t unheard of. Sometimes the power in certain generators would just snap. Mrs Rivers stuck her head out the hallway door
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93The power hasn\'92t gone out in the halls, it\'92s just our classroom. Let\'92s see\'85Mira, head down to the engine room and tell the staff that out generator has stopped working\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira sighed, she knew why she was being sent down and not any of her other classmates. Her and Ocean were one of the only students in the entire school from the lower levels, their excellent levels in all the subjects had granted them a ticket up a level education wise. But despite her frustration, she stood up and walked out of the classroom, headed out the hall and walked by the Main Street until she saw the massive spiral staircase in front of her.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira made her way down the huge staircase. I hate walking down these stairs, they are so large and unsettling, especially when it is so dark. Mira had recalled the time she left school late, when everything was dark, and fell down these same spiral stairs.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 The lower Mira went, the eerier it felt and it became darker as she gradually got farther from the sunlight that could be seen through the glass at the top. There was rust, cobwebs, and dirt everywhere. As she reached the last floor, the sunlight from the glass panel at the top couldn\'92t even be seen.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 At the bottom, she could not even see the door she needed to go to, all she could see was a luminescent sign that said "personnel only\'94, and a shiny reflective handle below it.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira assumed that this was the room that the teacher had mentioned, the engine room.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 It was her first time being sent down. Power outages happen quite often in the tank, usually caused by wildlife and oceanic animals outside the tank.With limited power within the societies, the government had to prioritize some departments over others.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Excuse me? The power\'92s out in Archimedes, I was sent down to ask for a reactivation.\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Hello? Anyone there?\'94 Mira repeated. The room stayed dark, and Mira turned on her flashlight. She made her way over to the desk on the other side of the room, and started inspecting them for a sign of relief reassuring her that she was on the right floor.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Final Radiation Report C-137, she read on the front page of the folder, along with a red warning saying \'93confidential information\'94. Oh wow, this is exactly what we were learning about. Couldn\'92t hurt to take a look if I'm already here.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 All information is shared in the tank, and secrets are only kept by the President and her direct connections. As she passed through the tens of pages in the folder, one of them caught her attention. It said \'93Radiation Levels: 3100, March 8th\'94, below it, there was a chart, with the radiation levels gathered from last week, along with radiation levels from the last five years. They all read\'85 \'930\'94.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 At the end of the page, it read; \'93FINDINGS: RADIATION LEVELS ARE AT ZERO, NO PRIOR EVIDENCE OF RADIATION FOUND.\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 What!? No radiation? How can that be? This cannot be right. Mira tries to forget the occurrence, but keeps it in the back of her mind. She promptly realises that she\'92s on the wrong floor when she sees the president\'92s team walk into the room, sending her out to clear the room for \'93official business\'94.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira finally arrives at the right floor and talks with the worker in the reflective vest. She promptly gets the power turned back on and returns to the school, but she still wonders if the radiation report could have had some sense.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Throughout the day, it was all she could think about. She had been learning about it just a few weeks ago in Mrs. Rivers class. There had been a mass nuclear bomb which\'92s large amounts of radiation had made life on the surface unsuitable for humans, that\'92s why they were even in the tank!
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 As weeks went by Mira couldn\'92t stop thinking about what had happened, things that she had never questioned before suddenly made no sense to her. She knew the nuclear bomb had caused humans to go under water. But when did the governments have time to build the Silo? Or when she was reading the reports, she saw a name for something or someone that she had never seen before, \'91Ocean\'92, and she knew for a fact that they weren\'92t talking about her best friend, so what was that? The ocean?
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 All of these thoughts were constantly gnawing at her conscience, she needed to tell someone, not her parents, they were both too old and tired from all the hard physical labour that low-rank workers had to do during their life, to now have to deal with their daughters conspiracy theories, she couldn\'92t tell Ocean either, if what she found out could endanger her, she didn\'92t want to risk Ocean, not her. Maybe she could talk to Grayson, her baby brother, he was so young, he wouldn\'92t remember or understand, her parents had waited a long time between her and her brother to fill the two child per family minimum policy.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira was starting to feel that crippling sense of desperation, the secret weighing heavy on her chest, dragging her every word, lacing all of her steps with that growing feeling of isolation. Then a person she hadn\'92t even considered popped into her mind, Torin. Mira knew that apart from owning his shop, he was also one of the divers that did maintenance work outside of the Tank, maybe she could talk to him, perhaps he\'92d even noticed these things too the last time he\'92d gone outside into the water.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She knew that he had been excused from his labor because of an incident where he had wounded himself with the equipment, and he had been rushed to the hospital of the middle level by his coworkers. So the department of health of The Silo had given him one of only two reasons to take a leave of absence: pregnancy or injury & sickness.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira tries to continue with her life as normal, dismissing the incident as something she simply read wrong. Since she wasn't supposed to see the document, it might have been a mistake, or referring to a different measure. Even though she made up her mind, a small part of her remained skeptical, wondering if there was some truth to it. The documents were technical and full of units that she didn't even know, and she wasn't even in the right room.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Weeks had passed since the blackout and Mira returned to her routine. A Tuna sandwich from Torin, school, the staircase. Everything went along well. It was a Friday when the lights went out again. The school went into a panic and the classroom became dark. Murmurs and questions flooded the air. Mrs. Rivers looked around the classroom and she decided on a girl in the second row.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Sara, go down and let them know that our generator isn't working.\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Sara got up immediately without a word, she had been down before. She was the type of student that was always prepared and never late. Mira watched her leave, happy to be chosen again. Mrs Rivers went back to her chair. Everyone was accustomed to the outages, being the consequences of living underwater. Twenty minutes later, the lights came back on, and cheers erupted in the classroom. But something, or someone was missing. Sara didn\'92t come back.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mrs. Rivers checked the door three times, and decided to keep teaching. She could have stopped somewhere, she thought. Maybe a teacher was talking to her. After ten more minutes Ocean whispered into Mira\'92s ear, and quietly said, \'93Where is she?\'94. Mira didn\'92t have an answer to give her. By the end of the class, she wasn\'92t the only one that noticed, and everyone started to get worried. Guesses flooded everywhere. Jack said he had seen her trip on the stairs before. Another student said she often got lost.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mrs Rivers told the classroom that the tank\'92s administrative team was handling it, putting an end to the discussion. By the end of the day, the school looked for any and all remaining explanations, but none of them came to fruition. While she was walking home, Mira checked the announcement boards on the wall at City Hall but there was nothing about Sara. On her way to school the next day, she checked again. No notice, announcement, or broadcast about the missing girl.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira, like everyone, tried to think of an explanation. There were procedures she didn\'92t know about, she thought. But after days of deliberation, it didn\'92t help get rid of the feeling she had, the one that said that something bad happened. Ocean started talking, but Mira wasn\'92t listening, she was planning something out.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Hey! Mira!\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93You haven\'92t heard a word I\'92ve said in three days\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Im fine\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93You look like when Torin was sick.\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira almost burst out. She was so close to saying what she wanted to say but she pushed it down, like she never had before. She thought about Sara\'92s empty chair.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Just tired\'94 she replied, trying to stay calm.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She was planning something out, which wasn\'92t like her. She normally made her decisions right before making them, reckless, unpredictable. She waited for the exact right lesson, not\'a0 the right moment. In the middle of something slow and long. History of Humanity should do it. Mira raised her hand and asked to go to the bathroom. Miss Rivers nodded. Mira went out into the corridor, right past the cubicles, past the portrait of Veyr ordered to be in every room.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She went down the staircases, across long hallways. Level by level, the light was getting thinner, the walls colder, and she knew she was approaching the underground. She stopped at the last civilian area, but went past the NO ENTER door, entering a sort of intermediary door, between an unmarked office, and the entrance. She realised there were people inside, and silently put her ear to the door and started to listen. She stayed incredibly still, knowing that one wrong breath could bust her plan wide open.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She heard voices, two men.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93We can\'92t keep patching the reports. Veyr\'92s office wants a full surface reading by next quarter. If they check the readings themselves-\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Don\'92t worry, they never have and never will. Besides, this only benefits them.\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Kennedy never even read the reports. Veyr does, and will. If she reads the last five years.
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93We will manage, like always.\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93It\'92s been 340 years, don\'92t you think it will all fall apart someday\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Someday, that\'92s another person\'92s problem, just focus on now.\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93One person. If just one single person finds out that there has been no radiation up there since before our grandparents were born and it's done. Everything falls apart.\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira leaned closer, her ear pushing against the door.
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 It opened, and she collapsed inside.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 "Hey! What are you doing here?"
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira gasped, her eyes widening. She realised that it was over, she had been caught.
\fs24 \strokec2 \

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 The two men restrained her, and she was dragged away deeper into the tank, where she had never been before.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\
\
}